Default transaction rollback for RuntimeExceptions

-----------------------------------------------------------

In its default configuration, the Spring Framework's transaction infrastructure code only marks a transaction for rollback in
the case of runtime, unchecked exceptions; that is, when the thrown exception is an instance or subclass of RuntimeException.
(Errors will also - by default - result in a rollback).
 Checked exceptions that are thrown from a transactional method do not result in rollback in the default configuration

