Difference between Interface and Abstract Class in Java 9 :
( post Java 8 , because now we got default methods and static methods available in Interface.. )
  *  Java 9 interfaces still cannot contain constructors. ( Abstract class can have constructors to init non static variables.. )
  *  Java 9 interfaces still cannot have non-static members ( Abstract class can have instance vars, event private instance vars but we can't say new on abstract so available to derived classes )
The key difference is that abstract class can maintain state but the interface cannot, and an abstract class can also have a constructor which is not allowed inside interface even in Java 8. If you are designing API then use interface and if you are abstracting both state and behaviour then use an abstract class.
