ConcurrentModificationException:
Now default List,Map,Set implementations are not thread safe so every mutation operation ( eg. remove, add ) causes internal
modcount variable to change, so iterator detects this throws exp ( as more that one iterators are not supported as he will not know which
element to skip or add in iteration.. ) but if it the only one then it know which elements removed.. added so iteration can safely done.
Scenarios:
1) calling collection's remove,add,set.. ( any mutation method) from multiple threads and No one is using iterators ( to read or write simultaneously ) : No exceptions as default methods don't throw exception ( they will only increment count.. ) but final collection will be unknown if its not thread safe
No exception even if multiple threads are calling remove , as default methods dont throw exp. ( so we can;t detect corruption.. )
2) calling default remove,set methods while some other thread is iterating over it :
Now as modcount has changed, Iterator methods will detect this and as expected_count != mod_count iterator methods will throw
ConcurrentModificationException ..
3) Only One iterator is using collection :
We can safely use iterators remove or other mutation methods and as iterator knows what has happened with collection
it can safely handle this.
4) Multiple iterators using same collection and modifying it : This is not supported and will result in ConcurrentModificationException
5) some default methods of collection also throw ConcurrentModificationException eg. sort . ( so iterators methods and some default methods only throw ConcurrentModificationException )
So always use iterators while read from non thread safe collection &amp; if other threads write to it.. atleast iterator will throw error,
but if we use normal collection methods we will never know that &amp; may read corrupt data..
Why collection has method remove and Iterators also have remove ??
=&gt; in non thread safe collection -&gt; calling remove from multiple threads makes collection corrupt but they don't even report that while iterators
remove at least throws exp.
If we want to use multiple threads for concurrent read,write then use ConcurrentCollections like ConcurrentHashMap,
CopyOnWriteArrayList..
