WeakHashMap: In Normal map when we set key or value null after putting it in map.. as map still points to the object, until map lives
those objects doesn't get garbage collected.. so in WeakHashMap as soon as we make key or value or both to null then can get
garbage collected even it map is pointing to them.
Java has 3 references: Strong, Soft &amp; Weak
Strong is the default one.. that we use day to day life. Object which is referenced through strong reference wont be garbage collected early
Soft Reference: Similar like Strong but these get garbage collected only when there is absolute memory requirements ( lazy gc )
eg.
Integer prim=1;&nbsp;
SoftReference&lt;Integer&gt; soft =new SoftReference&lt;Integer&gt;(prime); 
prime =null;
Weak : When these gets null, as soon as next GC runs these get garbage collected. ( eager GC )
Integer prime = 1;&nbsp;
WeakReference&lt;Integer&gt; soft = new WeakReference&lt;Integer&gt;(prime);
prime = null;
WeakReference&nbsp;type are used as Key in&nbsp;WeakHashMap
So as soon as we make key that is put in map already null.. in next GC it gets garbage collected and entry ( whole entry ) is gone from map
maps size reduces as GC.
