Why String is immutable ?
1) Java caches strings in String pool which is ConcurrentHashMap whose key is String that is being cached, so if string is mutable then 
its hashcode will change &amp; this will break hash map's functionality
2) Security Reasons: As string is used in urls , db connection urls and others, immutability makes these safe
3) Immutability gives thread safety
