HATEOASHypermedia as the Engine of Application State
Principle : API should guide the client through the application by returning relevant information about the next potential steps,
along with each response.
The response contains these possible follow-up links: make a deposit, withdrawal, or transfer, or close the account.
When the account information is retrieved later, the account is overdrawn:
Now only one link is available: to deposit more money. In its current&nbsp;state, the other links are not available. Hence the term&nbsp;Engine of Application State. What actions are possible varies as the state of the resource varies.
This is a very powerful mechanism, allowing client and server to be developed independently and it creates great possibilities like dynamically directing to another server without any changes in the client. 
You use it to gain loose coupling and evolvability by creating a generic interface. But if your clients don’t use your API in the correct way, HATEOAS becomes completely useless.
