Async Spring and Many more
Key Points:
supplyAsync (accepts supplier) , thenApplyAsync ( accepts function ), thenAcceptAsync ( accepts consumer )
each method is a stage in execution steps returns CompletableFuture&lt;some object or Void if its consumer&gt;
Then we can call get to block main thread. or return that CompletableFuture from controller of spring.
This releases req. processing thread much faster and its ready to process next req. while in background ForkJoinPool
does the execution of these callables and on completion sets data in CompletableFuture.
Spring Event polling thread tracks all these CompletableFuture object which are returned from Controller and
check whether data is arrived or not if its arrived then writes result back to connection and its done.
Spring also has @EnableAsyc thing to make controller , service methods to return CompletableFuture directly just annotating them by @Async so if its simple logic and not multiple async steps then can use this.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Problem with threads :
A thread can't have parameters and can't return value , even can't throw checked exception as All threads implement
Runnable so this restriction is solved by Callable.
Callable :
These threads still can't accept parameters directly but can return value also can throw checked Exceptions.
Lets consider scenario that you want to run various tasks serially i.e after one completes next gets executed and results passed between them, or parallel or some steps serially and some parallel and some serial again but the issue is there was no way to do this and if you try to write complex logic then may end up blocking the main thread which defeats purpose.
Callable function returns Future object, we can check this to know whether callable completed and value is in there or not
CompletableFuture :
Here we give callables / runnables to execute either on same thread if we dont use Async version methods or if we use Async version methods then they get executed on ForkJoin.commonPool() i.e common thread pool created by ForkJoin class internally
Java 8 introduced the&nbsp;CompletableFuture&nbsp;class.&nbsp;Along with the&nbsp;Future&nbsp;interface, it also implemented the&nbsp;CompletionStage&nbsp;interface. This interface defines the contract for an asynchronous computation step that we can combine with other steps.
with&nbsp;about 50 different methods for composing, combining, and executing asynchronous computation steps and handling errors.
public Future&lt;String&gt; calculateAsync() throws InterruptedException {
&nbsp;&nbsp;CompletableFuture&lt;String&gt; completableFuture = new CompletableFuture&lt;&gt;();
&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;Executors.newCachedThreadPool().submit(() -&gt; {
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Thread.sleep(500);
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;completableFuture.complete("Hello");
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return null;
&nbsp;&nbsp;});
&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;return completableFuture;
}
Future&lt;String&gt; CompletableFuture.completedFuture("Done");
Future&lt;String&gt; CompletableFuture.failedFuture(new Exception());
Optionally we can manually complete or fail future. so call on future.get() will return immediately.
Static methods&nbsp;runAsync&nbsp;and&nbsp;supplyAsync&nbsp;allow us to create a&nbsp;CompletableFuture&nbsp;instance out of&nbsp;Runnable&nbsp;and&nbsp;Supplier&nbsp;functional types correspondingly.
CompletableFuture&lt;String&gt; future
&nbsp;= CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -&gt; "Hello");
&nbsp;
// ...
&nbsp;
assertEquals("Hello", future.get());
thenApply : This is to chain multiple tasks and result of previous task is feed ed to next task. If previous task fails i.e throws
exception then all next chained tasks will be cancelled.
CompletableFuture&lt;String&gt; completableFuture
&nbsp;= CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -&gt; "Hello");
&nbsp;
CompletableFuture&lt;String&gt; future = completableFuture
&nbsp;.thenApply(s -&gt; s + " World");
&nbsp;
assertEquals("Hello World", future.get());
thenAccept : If we dont has further tasks and now want to chain last task thenAccept accepts consumer and returns void.
So if we use this method then CompletableFuture will return nothing, so we need to put all relevent logic in thenAccept method itself.
CompletableFuture&lt;String&gt; completableFuture = CompletableFuture
        .supplyAsync(() -&gt; "Hello")
        .supplyAsync(() -&gt; " World");
Above CompletableFuture returns String but this will get processed on main thread, so try to use thenAccept() always.
If we use multiple supplyAsync then we only get result of last supplyAsync in thenAccept, previous ones will execute but we
will not get result.
thenCompose method is used to chain two&nbsp;Futures&nbsp;sequentially.
thenApply vs thenCompose :
We can use CompletableFuture.allOf to combine multiple futures.
Now what happens when exception is raised ?
We can use handle((ret_data, exception) -&gt; {... return something}) method to handle exception async way or we can return back that result through future object .get() method. so in case of handle we get the data returned by handle method.
If we want to catch and do something about exception then we can use completeExceptionally()
